  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 405.05 Application Procedures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 405.05 Application Procedures.\n\n(a) An applicant requesting approval to construct or register a new small CWS or reactivate a small CWS shall submit a complete application, as specified in (b) below, to the department electronically at dwengineering@des.nh.gov.\n\n(b) An application shall be submitted in 2 parts, part I, concept approval, and part II, as follows:\n\n(1) Part I shall be completed as specified in Env-Dw 405.06, and part II shall be completed as specified in Env-Dw 405.09;\n\n(2) Part I of the design review application required by Env-Dw 405.06 shall be submitted and approved by the department prior to submission of the preliminary well report specified in Env-Dw 302 or Env-Dw 305; and\n\n(3) Part II shall not be submitted until part I has been approved by the department and all new sources required as part of the design have been approved by the department in accordance with Env-Dw 302, Env-Dw 305, or both, as applicable.\n\n(c) An applicant requesting approval to modify, expand, or enlarge an existing small CWS shall submit the following to the department electronically at dwengineering@des.nh.gov:\n\n(1) The name, location, and PWS identifier;\n\n(2) The name, mailing address, daytime telephone number, and e-mail address of the contact person who can answer questions about the proposal on behalf of the owner; and\n\n(3) The information required in Env-Dw 405.31.\n\n(d) The plans and specifications for all proposed small CWSs or modifications, including expansions, to existing small CWSs with a design flow greater than 20,000 gpd or with 50 or more service connections shall be sealed by a professional engineer licensed in the state of New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #14158, eff 12-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
}
